WEBVTT

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:00.204
about intuition. It also gave me

00:01:00.204 --> 00:01:02.871
a new way of thinking about which
ideas are worth pursuing.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.913
Since Danny is an expert
on decision making,

00:01:06.246 --> 00:01:09.788
I thought I'd start by asking about what
we're seeking in so many of our decisions.

00:01:10.621 --> 00:01:14.621
You've spent a lot of your career studying
happiness and related topics.

00:01:15.121 --> 00:01:18.246
And really, for the first
time in my career,

00:01:18.246 --> 00:01:21.204
I started to wonder why are we
so obsessed with happiness

00:01:21.204 --> 00:01:25.413
as psychologists? You know, I'm all
for people leading enjoyable,

00:01:25.413 --> 00:01:28.829
satisfying lives. But if I had to choose,

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:33.288
I would much rather have people focus
on character and, you know,